`selexprep_catalog.csv` is the canonical flat source used to build the
`selexprep_public_catalog` package dataset. It contains 240 public HT-SELEX
deposits from ENA, Figshare, and Zenodo, with eight curated experimental fields
and a reconciliation status for each field.

The snapshot was migrated byte-for-byte from the original Python project. Run
`inst/scripts/make-selexprep-public-catalog.R` from the package source root to
verify its SHA-256, schema, identifiers, and statuses before rebuilding the
`.rda` dataset.

The package code is MIT-licensed. The catalog is factual public-record metadata;
the underlying records and publications remain subject to their originating
terms. See `inst/CATALOG_PROVENANCE.md` for sources, curation disclosure, and
immutable provenance links.

This is a frozen discovery snapshot, not a live availability claim. Before
downloading ENA data, use `inspect_selexprep_accession()` to obtain current
records and verify that an accession is still available.
